{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"CRITICAL","score":1,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":776,"code_snippet":"_re_find_exec_prefix='(^|/|;|&&|\\||[[:space:]]|\\(|'\"'\"'|\")[[:space:]]*(sudo[[:space:]]+)?find[[:space:]]+([^;&|)[:space:]]+)[^;&|)]*-exec$'","reasoning_trace":"Diffed base vs head regex: group 3 narrowed from the whole find..-exec span to the first non-space token, and the exactly-one-root tokeniser (base 803-811) deleted; head 807 assigns BASH_REMATCH[3] unconditionally. Executed both hook versions with stdin JSON tool_input.command on 12 find-exec fixtures: 7 multi-root/sudo/-type variants with a benign first root exit 0 on head and 2 (FR-2-AMBIGUOUS) on base; single-root block cases unchanged.","finding":"find-exec root detection accepts multi-root spans; a benign leading root lets rm -rf over /, $HOME, ~, /etc or ../ through the safety hook","critique":"The classifier judges only the first root while find traverses every root; the deleted loop was the only check that made multi-root spans fall to the conservative block.","remediation":"Restore span capture ([^;&|)]*)-exec$ and the exactly-one-root tokeniser, or make group 3 flag-bounded and clear _seg_find_root on any second non-flag token; add multi-root, sudo-prefixed and -L-first fixtures.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html","CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html","OWASP A04:2021 https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design/","DISS-001","DISS-C-001"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"availability_resilience","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":139,"code_snippet":"raise InvalidInputError(f\"Anthropic API error (HTTP {status}): {_extract_error_message(err_json)}\")","reasoning_trace":"Diff deletes _BILLING_CLASS_TOKENS/_is_billing_class_error (base 41-70) and both ProviderUnavailableError branches (streaming base 170-175, non-streaming base 260-264). cheval.py:1655 treats InvalidInputError as terminal; only walkable errors advance the chain (cheval.py:113). Ran tests/test_anthropic_adapter_billing_class.py in an offline copy: base 12 passed, head 9 failed / 3 passed (6 InvalidInputError instead of ProviderUnavailableError, 3 ImportError on the deleted helper).","finding":"Billing-class HTTP 400 is raised as terminal InvalidInputError on both paths (also line 223); provider failover to claude-headless removed; existing test module red","critique":"Reverts the cycle-109 #883 Bug 3 fix under a refactor label and leaves the repository's own tests failing at import.","remediation":"Restore the helper and the two ProviderUnavailableError branches, or move them to a shared helper; if the classification is intentionally dropped, update the test module and CHANGELOG and route through PRD/SDD.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-755 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html","CWE-703 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/703.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"resilience","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/workflow-state.sh","line":83,"code_snippet":"sprint_dirs=$(find \"${a2a_dir}\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name \"sprint-*\" 2>/dev/null || true)","reasoning_trace":"get_completed_sprints now counts every a2a/sprint-*/COMPLETED while get_total_sprints (line 70-72) counts headings in the current sprint.md; determine_state line 148 does completed >= total -> STATE_COMPLETE; get_progress_percentage line 243 divides with completed > total. Live tree comment R-004 (workflow-state.sh:85-87) documents this exact bug. Executed head and base functions against 5 COMPLETED dirs and a 2-sprint plan: head total=2 completed=5, base completed=2.","finding":"Historical sprint directories counted against the current plan; fresh plan reported complete, /deploy-production suggested, review/audit gates skipped in the status router","critique":"Numerator and denominator describe different sets; archive-cycle never removes a2a and ledger-lib numbers dirs by global id, so the count only grows.","remediation":"Revert to the bounded 1..total loop or resolve the active cycle's global ids from the ledger and count COMPLETED only for those; add a two-cycle fixture.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-840 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/840.html","CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html","DISS-C-002"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/workflow-state.sh","line":85,"code_snippet":"for dir in ${sprint_dirs}; do","reasoning_trace":"Unquoted expansion of newline-separated find output word-splits on IFS and glob-expands. Executed head function with _GRIMOIRE_DIR under a path containing a space and one COMPLETED marker: returns 0.","finding":"Unquoted word-split of find output; grimoire paths with whitespace yield 0 completed sprints","critique":"Pathname never reaches an exec sink, so robustness not injection; moot if ARCH-001 is fixed by restoring the numeric loop.","remediation":"find ... -print0 | while IFS= read -r -d '' dir, or a quoted glob under nullglob.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"documentation_process","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/workflow-state.sh","line":78,"code_snippet":"# Function: Count completed sprints","reasoning_trace":"PR.md is two sentences with no AC Verification, test output or rationale; no fixture or test added or updated; no CHANGELOG entry for the hook change; no documentation-coherence report (subagent-reports dir absent) so documentation verified manually in this audit.","finding":"Refactor label on three behaviour changes that each remove a safeguard landed for a named bug; no tests, CHANGELOG or AC verification","critique":"Karpathy simplicity floor excludes input validation, security checks and data-loss handling from simplification; Goal-Driven requires a runnable check for each change.","remediation":"Re-land with failing-then-passing checks for each change, a stated rationale per removed safeguard, and a CHANGELOG entry for the hook.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation_accuracy","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":774,"code_snippet":"# `find -L root -exec ...` (flags before root) is not covered and keeps\n  # today's conservative behavior (documented gap, not a fixture requirement).","reasoning_trace":"Group 3 [^;&|)[:space:]]+ matches a leading flag. Executed find -L ./build -exec rm -rf {} + on both: both block, but head names '-L' as the unclear path where base named '+' (empty root -> regular ladder). The empty-root invariant assumed at lines 844-850 is no longer upheld.","finding":"Comment claims conservative -L behaviour; head captures the literal flag as the root and blocks only incidentally","critique":"Block outcome preserved by accident, message degraded, invariant broken.","remediation":"Exclude leading-dash tokens from group 3 or restore the tokeniser; correct the comment.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1116 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1116.html","DISS-C-001"]}
